  "summary": "The spider is built and renders, but I haven't seen the walk cycle play. Typecheck passes. The render tool returns one still frame, and that frame shows the whole spider with soft shadows on a light gray studio ground from a three-quarter camera. The render report flagged `FRAME_EMPTY` (only 8.9% of the frame textured), but that only reflects how much of the plain backdrop is flat. The spider itself rendered correctly.\n\nThe spider is `recipes/spider.mjs`, imported with `import_three`. It has an abdomen, thorax, head, eyes and fangs, all made from spheres and cones. Each of the eight legs has two cylinder segments joined by a knee sphere.\n\nOne 2-second clip drives the walk. The legs on opposite diagonals move together, and each leg lifts, swings forward and plants again. The body bobs twice per cycle, once per step. The first and last keyframes match, so the loop is seamless.\n\n`src/main.ts` mounts the scene, plays the clip and sets `window.__EVAL_READY__`. No external model files are loaded, and `src/` doesn't import `three`.\n\nI can't judge from the still whether the gait reads well. It would be worth a quick look in a browser.\n\n"
}